## Run and deploy

Install dependencies with `npm install` and start the app with `npm start`.

For local development, copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set `mongo_url` and
`mongodb_name` to match your MongoDB deployment. The app uses the host-provided
`PORT` when available, then falls back to `pro` and port `3000`.

For a Node.js hosting service, use `npm install` as the build command and
`npm start` as the start command. Configure `mongo_url` and `mongodb_name` as
environment variables in the host's settings; the host should provide `PORT`.
Do not commit `.env` or put database credentials in source control.